126 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 68 0 R
/T (Welcome to Issue 002 of ORBIT & ORIGIN. Scientific progress is frequently reported as a lightning strike: an observatory spots a new planet, an algorithm cracks the climate, or a biologist isolates a cure. Yet physical truth behaves much more subtly. In real laboratories and field stations, the decisive transition happens when faint patterns buried beneath instrumental noise and natural variability are teased out by a sound methodology.)
/E (Welcome to Issue 002 of ORBIT & ORIGIN. Scientific progress is frequently reported as a lightning strike: an observatory spots a new planet, an algorithm cracks the climate, or a biologist isolates a cure. Yet physical truth behaves much more subtly. In real laboratories and field stations, the decisive transition happens when faint patterns buried beneath instrumental noise and natural variability are teased out by a sound methodology.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
